# __PROJECT_NAME__

This project was generated by Dotisan as a standard ASP.NET Core + Vue/Vite application with EF Core __DATABASE_DISPLAY__ and opt-in ASP.NET Core Identity cookie authentication.

## Build and run

~~~powershell
dotnet build __PROJECT_NAME__.sln
dotnet run --project src\__PROJECT_NAME__.Api
~~~

Authentication is enabled because the project was created with `--auth yes`. The generated API exposes antiforgery, registration (when enabled), login/logout, and the current-user endpoint under `/api/account`.

The generated code uses normal ASP.NET Core Identity, EF Core, cookie authentication, dependency injection, and ProblemDetails. Review and extend these source files directly; Dotisan does not hide the authentication implementation behind a runtime framework.

The Vue portal includes ready-to-edit login, registration, forgot-password, and profile pages under `src\__PROJECT_NAME__.Web\src\pages`, composed from local shadcn-vue-style primitives. The authenticated portal shell keeps generated API contracts in `src\__PROJECT_NAME__.Web\src\dotisan` and application UI in `components`, `layouts`, and `pages`.

## Database and migrations

`dotisan dev` creates the `InitialCreate` migration when the project has none and applies all local development migrations before starting the API. This handles the first-run Identity schema automatically.

~~~powershell
dotisan dev
dotisan migrate
~~~

`dotisan migrate` applies existing migrations and remains the explicit production command. For production, author and review migrations with `dotnet ef migrations add` before applying them; `dotisan dev` never runs production migrations.

## Production configuration

Use normal ASP.NET Core configuration sources for the connection string and Identity settings. Do not commit production secrets or local SQLite databases. Run behind HTTPS, configure a durable data-protection key ring for multi-instance deployments, and keep cookie, antiforgery, password, lockout, and registration policies appropriate for the deployment environment.

## Frontend development

~~~powershell
cd src\__PROJECT_NAME__.Web
npm run dev
~~~

`dotisan new` installs frontend dependencies before reporting success. If the project was generated with `--no-restore`, run `npm install` or `pnpm install` before `npm run dev`.

After the wizard, Dotisan checks the .NET SDK, `dotnet-ef`, and the selected frontend package manager. Press Ctrl+C once while `dotisan dev` is running to stop the API and frontend together. Dotisan allows graceful shutdown before falling back to process-tree cleanup.

